description=Realistic, balanced traits, mostly negative, that add complications to work around: Alcoholic, Brittle, Arthritis, Caffeine Dependent, Migraines, Hemophilia, Anaemic, Major Depressive Disorder, A Really Bad Day, Hallucinations, Brittle Asthma, Gluten Intolerance, Vegetarian, Diabetes Type 1 and Type 2, Heart Condition, Epilepsy, Multiple Sclerosis, Tinnitus, Lactose Intolerance, Germaphobe, Straight Edge, Homebody, Sweaty, Sensitive Skin, Sensory Issues, ADHD and five fitness flaws, plus the positive Renaissance Faire Geek, Gym Regular, Early Riser, Meal Prepper, Deep Sleeper, Steady Hands, Night Shift, Hollow Legs, Fast Recovery, Good Clotter, Thick Skull, Grit, Nomad, Cool Customer, Slob, Homemaker and five fitness perks, reworked Smoker, Fear of Blood, Cat's Eyes, Outdoorsman and Resilient, and In Their 20s / 30s / 40s / 50s for the Age system with a trait or two of their own each. For everyone: Vitality (fresh food, exercise and sleep slowly earn small stat boosts, junk and neglect the reverse), fitness training (muscle groups that tire and recover, improvised weights, stretching, training plans), cooked meals that lift your mood and fuel training, sleep and light (and sleeping in your clothes), a home that does you good, laundry (washing floors, damp and musty clothes, stains, clotheslines), reading for pleasure (genres, long reads, tastes, the Good Read moodle, real 1993 books), hangovers and drink relief, sunburn (and sun block to keep it off) and dehydration, and a health overhaul (blood loss and shock, wound infection and antibiotics, wound care, what First Aid tells you, a blood readout, a medication reminder, concussion, passing out), most with a sandbox switch. Singleplayer only for now. The moodles need Moodle Framework.
